# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mizo Universe – Environment Variables Template
#
# HOW TO USE
# 1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env.local
# 2. Fill in the real values in .env.local (NEVER commit that file).
# 3. This file IS committed to source control – it must contain NO real secrets.
#
# NEXT.JS RULES
# • Variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are bundled into the client bundle and
#   visible to anyone who inspects your JavaScript.  Only put non-sensitive,
#   truly public values there (e.g. public analytics IDs, public API base URLs).
# • All other variables (no prefix) are available only on the server (SSR /
#   API routes / Server Actions / Route Handlers).  Put all secrets here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL (used for canonical links, OG meta, sitemap, etc.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mizo-universe.com

# ── Analytics (public – no secret) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Example: Replace with your own measurement ID if you add analytics.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Amplitude Experiment (public – deployment key, not a secret) ──────────────
# Obtain the deployment key from the Amplitude Experiment console:
#   Amplitude → Experiment → Deployments → <your deployment> → Deployment Key
# This key is safe to expose in the browser bundle (it has no secret value).
NEXT_PUBLIC_AMPLITUDE_DEPLOYMENT_KEY=replace-with-your-deployment-key

# ── External API secrets (server-side only – NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) ─────────
# Add any third-party API keys or secrets below.
# These are NEVER exposed to the browser.
# Example:
# MY_SECRET_API_KEY=replace-me
